/users/Zhang-Yingyi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"Zhang-Yingyi","id":66407808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NDA3ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66407808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi","html_url":"https://github.com/Zhang-Yingyi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zhang-Yingyi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"925ac64e7cf2c0f4b11990f0fac33224ef257520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/commits/925ac64e7cf2c0f4b11990f0fac33224ef257520","html_url":"https://github.com/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/commit/925ac64e7cf2c0f4b11990f0fac33224ef257520"}],"stats":{"total":537047,"additions":537045,"deletions":2},"files":[{"sha":"db6f3e19cd22c4f93eb263625b4c035f8105e2a5","filename":".DS_Store","status":"added","additions":0,"deletions":0,"changes":0,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/blob/d6a2cb3416e8320bcb1439921d319729aeccec8e/.DS_Store","raw_url":"https://github.com/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/raw/d6a2cb3416e8320bcb1439921d319729aeccec8e/.DS_Store","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/contents/.DS_Store?ref=d6a2cb3416e8320bcb1439921d319729aeccec8e"},{"sha":"5c895a46b472e43031f18068ad09478cfcf57c87","filename":"README.md","status":"modified","additions":107,"deletions":2,"changes":109,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/blob/d6a2cb3416e8320bcb1439921d319729aeccec8e/README.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/raw/d6a2cb3416e8320bcb1439921d319729aeccec8e/README.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/contents/README.md?ref=d6a2cb3416e8320bcb1439921d319729aeccec8e","patch":"@@ -1,5 +1,110 @@\n-# ICLR2026_RF-Mem\n+# Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval\n \n This repository contains the code and resources for the ICLR 2026 paper titled \"Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval\". \n \n-The origin code of submission can be found here: https://openreview.net/attachment?id=f7p0F2X6XN&name=supplementary_material.\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+The origin code of submission can be found here: https://openreview.net/attachment?id=f7p0F2X6XN&name=supplementary_material.\n+\n+\n+## 🧠 RF-Mem\n+\n+RF-Mem (**Recollection–Familiarity Memory**) is an adaptive retrieval framework for Large Language Models, grounded in the **dual-process theory of human cognition**.  \n+In cognitive science, memory is often described as a combination of two systems:  \n+\n+- **Familiarity** – fast, effortless recognition that something has been seen before.  \n+- **Recollection** – slower, deliberate reconstruction of episodic details such as time, place, and context.  \n+\n+This theory motivates RF-Mem: instead of treating retrieval as either one-shot search or full-context prompting, RF-Mem adaptively balances the two.  \n+\n+\n+![Intro](./RF_mem/assets/Intro.png)\n+\n+## 📊 Framework Overview\n+The RF-Mem framework first measures retrieval uncertainty using mean similarity and entropy.  \n+- If ths system feel familiarity, it selects the **Familiarity path** for direct retrieval.  \n+- If this system feel unfamiliar, it switches to the **Recollection path**, where memory items are clustered and iteratively expanded with query reformulation.  \n+\n+This dual-path design enables scalable and efficient personalized memory retrieval, improving both accuracy and efficiency across long-term memory benchmarks such as PersonaBench, PersonaMem, and LongMemEval.\n+\n+![Framework](./RF_mem/assets/framework.png)\n+\n+---\n+\n+\n+## 📂 Project Structure\n+\n+```\n+RF_mem\n+├──LongMemEval/.                # LongMemEval experiment data and scripts\n+│   ├──  assets/                # Figures of this paper\n+│   ├──  data/                  # Shared data directory\n+│   ├──  LICENSE\n+│   ├──  README.md              # Project description\n+│   ├──  requirements-full.txt  # Full dependencies\n+│   ├──  requirements-lite.txt  # Lightweight dependencies\n+│   ├──  run.sh                 # Quick start script\n+│\n+├── personabench_data/          # PersonaBench experiment data and scripts\n+│   ├── eval_data/              # Evaluation data\n+│   ├── llm_model/              # LLM model wrapper\n+│   ├── retri_mdoel/            # Retrieval model\n+│   ├── eval.py                 # PersonaBench evaluation entry\n+│   ├── main_batch.py           # Batch experiment entry\n+│   ├── run.sh                  # Quick run script\n+│   └── utils.py                # Utility functions\n+│\n+└── personamem_data/            # PersonaMem experiment data and scripts\n+    ├── apitokens/              # API key configuration\n+    ├── data/                   # Data directory\n+    ├── llm_model/              # LLM model wrapper\n+    ├── retri_mdoel/            # Retrieval model\n+    ├── main_batch.py           # PersonaMem batch experiment entry\n+    ├── run.sh                  # Quick run script\n+    └── utils.py                # Utility functions\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 🔧 Installation\n+\n+It is recommended to use Python 3.10+.\n+   ```bash\n+   pip install -r requirements.txt\n+   ```\n+\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 🚀 Usage\n+\n+\n+1. **Run LongMemEval experiments**\n+   ```bash\n+   cd LongMemEval\n+   bash run.sh\n+   ```\n+\n+\n+2. **Run PersonaBench experiments**\n+   ```bash\n+   cd personabench_data\n+   bash run.sh\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Run PersonaMem experiments**\n+   ```bash\n+   cd personamem_data\n+   bash run.sh\n+   ```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 📜 License\n+\n+This project is licensed under the [MIT License](LICENSE).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## ✨ Acknowledgements\n+\n+- Authors of LongMemEval, PersonaBench & PersonaMem datasets  \n+- OpenAI / HuggingFace model community  "},{"sha":"2e2c8491038bf0383c324a478b66a4663833efea","filename":"RF_mem/LongMemEval/LICENSE","status":"added","additions":21,"deletions":0,"changes":21,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/blob/d6a2cb3416e8320bcb1439921d319729aeccec8e/RF_mem%2FLongMemEval%2FLICENSE","raw_url":"https://github.com/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/raw/d6a2cb3416e8320bcb1439921d319729aeccec8e/RF_mem%2FLongMemEval%2FLICENSE","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Applied-Machine-Learning-Lab/ICLR2026_RF-Mem/contents/RF_mem%2FLongMemEval%2FLICENSE?ref=d6a2cb3416e8320bcb1439921d319729aeccec8e","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@\n+MIT License\n+\n+Copyright (c) 2024 Di Wu\n+\n+Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n+of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n+in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n+to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n+copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n+furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n+\n+The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n+